  "title": "The Smallest Eberlein Eigenvalue of J(4r+2,2r,r): The Sharp Threshold r0=2",
  "batch_label": "63",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every integer r >= 2, the full set of indices minimizing the Eberlein eigenvalues of J(4r+2,2r,r) is I(r)={2}. Consequently the least integer r0 >= 2 such that E_r(2) is a smallest adjacency eigenvalue for every r >= r0 is r0=2, and there are no exceptions in the range 2 <= r < r0.",
